                        "entry_id": "16d5cd49-098a-3a4e-b8db-8c30261115de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name from German or Hebrew."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d55518fd-981b-49e5-905d-65939e456f6d",
                                "sense_id": "bb4fb6e1-f32c-32e6-b086-a027c230e651",
                                "text": "A friend that I envied — it was the same friend who had benefited from admiring Cosette's jewelry, a girl whose name was Elsa and whom naturally we called Lioness —"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5ceefd5-2296-48ed-9aa2-54471d3553b2",
                                "sense_id": "bb4fb6e1-f32c-32e6-b086-a027c230e651",
                                "text": "Do you remember the wave of Elsas that arrived shortly after the release of Frozen at the end of 2013? It became one the fastest-climbing names of the following year before dropping back, and then had another (smaller) spike in 2019 when Frozen II came out."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
